            <ArticleTitle>Treatment update for allergic rhinitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This manuscript addresses the pathogenesis of allergic rhinitis, use of nasal provocation as a method to assess inflammatory mediators and the role of cytokines, and topical glucocorticosteroids. Immunologic changes of allergen immunotherapy, pharmacotherapy with a focus on non-sedating, and topical antihistamines are discussed. The antiinflammatory potential of fexofenadine, azelastine, and newer therapeutic modalities with anti-IgE are addressed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
